            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for wrath, then the Malayalam for to be upset."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഭയം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭയം — bhayaṁ — \"dread; fear\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുട്ടിക്ക് ഇരുട്ടിനെ ഭയമായിരുന്നു. kuṭṭikkŭ iruṭṭine bhayamāyirunnu. The child was afraid of the dark."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Written and formal; in speech പേടി is more usual. The one afraid takes -ക്ക്, the thing feared -എ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭയം (bhayaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit bhaya, \"fear, peril\", from the root bhī, \"to fear\" (CDIAL 9390)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
