          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഏകാന്തത (ēkāntata) is borrowed from Sanskrit ekānta, \"a lonely or retired place\" (Monier-Williams), with the noun ending -tā. The Sanskrit word joins eka, \"one\", and anta, \"end, side\"."
            }
          ]
